not sure about that one. From my reading of the code that's only possible if someone set non-default option `runtime-validate-json`.


And even then it would not just drop these properties, it would drop the entire config file?

```
  void Configuration::loadSingleConfigFile(const std::filesystem::path& jsonPath,
                                           const nlohmann::json& schema)
  {
      std::ifstream jsonStream(jsonPath.c_str());
      if (!jsonStream.good())
      {   
          lg2::error("unable to open {PATH}", "PATH", jsonPath.string());
          return;
      }   
      auto data = nlohmann::json::parse(jsonStream, nullptr, false, true);
      if (data.is_discarded())
      {   
          lg2::error("syntax error in {PATH}", "PATH", jsonPath.string());
          return;
      }   

      if (ENABLE_RUNTIME_VALIDATE_JSON && !validateJson(schema, data))
      {   
          lg2::error("Error validating {PATH}", "PATH", jsonPath.string());
          return;
      }   

      if (data.type() == nlohmann::json::value_t::array)
      {   
          for (auto& d : data)
          {
              configurations.emplace_back(d);
          }   
      }   
      else
      {   
          configurations.emplace_back(data);
      }   
  }
```

Can you help me to understand which code path caused the behavior you are describing or alternatively remove the section from commit message.
